#+TITLE: Windows upgrade selects stale libredwg.dll instead of the shim import
#+STATUS: NEXT
#+PRIORITY: P1
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: -
#+DATE: 2026-10-28

* Verified deployment regression

After upgrading Windows from clautolisp/ALFE 2.3.23 to the 2.3.75 release
built from upstream 1ad230be, version checks pass but VLA-SAVEAS fails with
COM-SAVE-FAILED / no usable DWG native library. The release archives pass
scripts/test-windows-release.ps1 on a fresh prefix on pfenny. The installed
prefix on winservadm fails the same test with HOME absent and only Windows
on PATH.

The libraries archive contains clal_dwg.dll and msys-redwg.dll. Its shim's
PE import table names msys-redwg.dll (checked with objdump -p). The old
prefix also has libredwg.dll, retained by run-forest-run's merge installer.
The error identifies THAT obsolete file as the dependency it cannot load.

| File | SHA-256 in installed prefix |
| clal_dwg.dll (new archive) | 03396fc4afa84778bdff029c44b2186fb4438112b3cf35be1e145fa6b84891e2 |
| msys-redwg.dll (new archive) | 2573a26e5da1206d63d231544df3a668f2d4173d8c0fcee87fc462a4076dc85b |
| libredwg.dll (obsolete) | c63ce812ab2d6515c7fbb3553fbbadcee4a33a942b2642d7fb5e52e4deacd692 |

* Minimal runtime operation

The native release test loads this operation in clautolisp, without a CAD:

#+begin_src lisp
(vl-load-com)
(setq d (vla-get-activedocument (vlax-get-acad-object)))
(vla-addline (vla-get-modelspace d)
             (vlax-3d-point 0.0 0.0 0.0)
             (vlax-3d-point 10.0 10.0 0.0))
(vla-saveas d "native.dwg")
#+end_src

Use a disposable prefix extracted from the binaries and libraries ZIPs.
Reproduce the upgrade state by adding the old libredwg.dll beside the new
shim under lib/clautolisp/windows/x86-64, then run the native release test
with -Prefix. Do not add an obsolete DLL to a production prefix.

* Cause

clautolisp/drawing-dwg/source/bindings.lisp:
%libredwg-dependency-in picks the FIRST filename containing redwg;
%libredwg-dependency-beside passes directory results directly to it.
%try-load-shim preloads that arbitrary file rather than the shim's actual
PE dependency. Several toolchain filenames can coexist after an upgrade;
matching a substring does not identify the required library.

* Verified workaround and result

Moved only the obsolete libredwg.dll outside the prefix, preserving its
hash and file for diagnosis. No executable or current DLL was changed.
The same installed-prefix test then passes all five checks, including
NATIVE-DWG-SAVED; the XRecord/PKPM reproducer also passes. This confirms
an upgrade-prefix selection problem, not a missing DLL in the new ZIP.

* Acceptance

- Select the actual shim dependency (for example via build/install metadata
  or PE imports), handling toolchain-dependent names without choosing an
  arbitrary older library by directory order.
- Add an upgrade test with two redwg DLL spellings, including an unusable
  stale candidate before the current one. Verify the current import loads
  and a DWG is written with only Windows on PATH.
- Keep fresh-prefix native release tests and cover the installed-prefix
  upgrade path; do not rely on a developer workspace fallback.
- Coordinate package-owned obsolete-file cleanup with run-forest-run;
  do not remove unrelated installed libraries.
